<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="11603c26">&lt;p&gt;
    This work product provides overall context and approach for the change initiative as well as detailed approach content
    for business readiness and business adoption.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Engagement
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    This section defines the strategic actions for how to work with stakeholders to accept and be involved in managing
    the changes in their business. This section provides guidelines for stakeholder engagement planning, related
    events, and activities to set the direction and achieve agreement among sponsors for how stakeholders will be moved
    through the change process with engaging events, communications, networks. This section also sets forth how
    feedback, relevant issues, and concerns, will be addressed on an ongoing basis.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Readiness
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    This section describes the guiding principles and high-level activities needed to be conducted by the business /
    for the business to prepare their leaders, teams, and individuals to transition and adopt business changes.
    This section also outlines the key activities that the business needs to take to ready themselves for
    training and adopting the solution and facilitate the transfer of ownership for change from the program to the
    business.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;
    Business Adoption
&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    This section provides the milestones and process flow for validating adoption criteria with the business.
    This section also includes how to engage with the various stakeholder groups and a description of how status will be
    reported.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="ed00b996"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="2eff194b"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="89e115c3"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="5762d3d1">&lt;p&gt;
    To achieve consensus with the client about the people change process: managing people through change, minimizing
    disruption to stakeholders, and enabling the business to assume ownership in early stages of the change initiative; so,
    the program is not only reactive by planned and systematic.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
